      en: "The Queen Elizabeth II Quay, commonly known as the Deep Water Quay, is the primary port facility of Sierra Leone, located in the capital city of Freetown. It is situated on the southern bank of the Sierra Leone River, which forms one of the world's largest natural deep-water harbors. Officially opened in the 1950s, the port serves as the central hub for the country's international trade. It handles nearly all imports, such as fuel, food, and machinery, as well as exports like cocoa, coffee, and minerals. In recent years, extensive modernization efforts have been undertaken, including the expansion of container terminals by international partners like Bolloré. These developments have significantly increased the port's capacity, making Freetown a competitive player in West African logistics. The port is not only an economic engine but also a strategic point for regional security and supply chains. Its infrastructure includes specialized berths for oil tankers and general cargo vessels. Despite challenges such as urban congestion, the Quay remains the lifeblood of the Sierra Leonean economy.",
      es: "Queen Elizabeth II Quay es un puerto de aguas profundas en Freetown, Sierra Leona, llamado así por la reina británica. El muelle se construyó en la década de 1960 y es un importante centro de transbordo para el comercio internacional del país. Ofrece atraques para barcos con un calado de hasta 12 metros y está equipado con modernas terminales de contenedores. El puerto gestiona la mayoría de las importaciones y exportaciones de Sierra Leona, incluidos productos agrícolas, minerales y bienes de consumo. A pesar de su importancia, sufre de congestión e infraestructura obsoleta. En los últimos años, se han llevado a cabo renovaciones para aumentar la eficiencia.",
